{"ts": "2026-09-23T07:07:47Z", "type": "prompt", "text": "There is an annoying bug / feature request. If I have different sessinons open, there is a spill on the file change check. So if in one window (session) the agent (or i) changed file_1 the control for session 2 will hit as well and ask for attestation of file_1 change, although sessions 2 never touched file_1\n\nCan you review and properly implement session specific file change?", "prev": "genesis", "hash": "85dc629db51256df7e846db8fe8407c0bbf568548bb3bc3c5badd16e7b1e75f6"}
{"ts": "2026-09-23T07:07:47Z", "type": "prompt", "text": "There is an annoying bug / feature request. If I have different sessinons open, there is a spill on the file change check. So if in one window (session) the agent (or i) changed file_1 the control for session 2 will hit as well and ask for attestation of file_1 change, although sessions 2 never touched file_1\n\nCan you review and properly implement session specific file change?", "prev": "85dc629db51256df7e846db8fe8407c0bbf568548bb3bc3c5badd16e7b1e75f6", "hash": "dded3f0b6008005d1551d676b8af971c3cdb0c55fbac6d83125d9cd33f373482"}
{"ts": "2026-09-23T07:13:44Z", "type": "plan_registered", "origin": "inline", "declared_files": ["src/archrev/worktree.py", "src/archrev/gitutil.py", "src/archrev/hooks.py", "src/archrev/adapters.py", "src/archrev/cli.py", "src/archrev/scaffold.py", "src/archrev/drift.py", "src/archrev/report/render.py", "src/archrev/report/template.html", "tests/test_worktree_scope.py", "tests/test_adapters.py", ".cursor/hooks.json", "README.md"], "chars": 960, "text": "Goal: session-specific file-change attribution so parallel sessions/windows (and hand edits) no longer spill into each other's final review. Approach: per-session working-tree checkpoints (content fingerprints of dirty files) at session start and around each of the session's own shell/MCP commands (before + after hooks); only changes that happen inside this session's command windows count as its unexplained changes / gate bypasses; everything else becomes a new background_changes bucket. Legacy sessions without checkpoints keep current behavior. Also makes CLI 'latest' binding favor the session whose shell hook just fired. Files: src/archrev/worktree.py (new), src/archrev/gitutil.py, src/archrev/hooks.py, src/archrev/adapters.py, src/archrev/cli.py, src/archrev/scaffold.py, src/archrev/drift.py, src/archrev/report/render.py, src/archrev/report/template.html, tests/test_worktree_scope.py (new), tests/test_adapters.py, README.md, .cursor/hooks.json", "amend": false, "prev": "dded3f0b6008005d1551d676b8af971c3cdb0c55fbac6d83125d9cd33f373482", "hash": "c18d39345b8b31f97b717a328d0a5a78b94c33a5f5d27f754b13b646dd77e31a"}
